Recover a Creo operation program as JSON with label_version=4, model, feats. Use the semantic_v4 contract: each feature has data, operation, pattern, optional absent. operation/pattern use op plus schema/values OR raw_xml OR empty=true. values is a list of [zero-based slot index, lexical string or null]. Omitted slots retain the frozen schema defaults (int=0, double=0.00, otherwise null). Only op values consistent with the XML are accepted. data uses v2 feature aliases; dims keep complete dimension objects. Geometry/sketch arrays may use {$table:[column names],rows:[[values]]}. Heterogeneous arrays may use {$records:[[layout columns]],rows:[[layout_index,values...]]}. Preserve IDs/references, constraints, geometric mappings and nondefault feature settings. Do not output provided_context fields in model; the caller supplies them. No snapshots or binary payloads. Unsupported XML forms use explicit raw_xml. BREP face indices are not Creo historical geometry IDs. Frozen feature defaults: {"st":0,"feat_visible":1,"group_id":0,"is_pattern_leader":false,"layer_ids":[],"par":[],"chld":[],"refs":[],"dims":[],"feat_params":[],"sk":null,"geom_items":[],"sub":"","pattern_axis_angle":0,"pattern_axis_geom_id":-1,"pattern_axis_geom_type":0,"pattern_axis_owner_feat_id":-1,"pattern_class":0,"pattern_elem_refs":[],"pattern_first_dir_increment":0,"pattern_first_dir_instances":0,"pattern_header_id":-1,"pattern_leader_id":-1,"pattern_member_ids":[],"pattern_second_dir_instances":0,"pattern_status":0}
Field aliases (original->label): {"model":{"features":"feats","material_name":"material","relations":"rel"},"feature":{"feat_id":"id","feat_number":"n","feat_type_name":"type","feat_type":"type_id","feat_name":"name","feat_status":"st","feat_subtype":"sub","parent_ids":"par","child_ids":"chld","dimensions":"dims","sketch":"sk","elem_refs":"refs"},"sketch":{"location_matrix":"m","intent_manager":"im","entities":"e","dimensions":"d","projection_refs":"pr","constraints":"c"},"entity":{"ent_type":"t","json_ent_id":"id"}}
absent lists default keys that did not exist in source and must not be injected.
XML may alternatively use tree=[tag,attributes,text,children]. e: expands to PRO_E_; x: expands to PRO_XML_; other tags unchanged. Leaf text is lexical string or null; compound text is null. Raw XML remains valid for unsupported structures.
